v {xschem version=3.4.7 file_version=1.2
* io_slice -- MACHINE-GENERATED by design/generate_periphery.py;
* do not hand-edit, re-run the generator (see design/README.md).
* One I/O slice (periphery record rows 3, 5-8, 10): 4 transmission-gate
* pass gates per bit line onto one shared pair (mbl/mblb) that feeds one
* latch sense amp and one write driver; D/WEN input flops on rising clk;
* Q register (flop clocked by q_clk, a read-only strobe, so Q holds
* across writes and idle cycles).
